\title{SingleSampleDrDimont: Integrating Single-Sample Multi-Omics Molecular Networks into 'DrDimont' Using LIONESS}
\description{
Molecular networks built from omics data, such as mRNA or protein expression, describe how molecules interact and can be used to study diseases. They are usually built for groups of patients or samples to describe a condition, which can hide the properties of an individual patient or sample behind the group average. The package enables individual-sample comparisons. It builds single-sample networks for one or more omics layers with the LIONESS method (Linear Interpolation to Obtain Network Estimates for Single Samples) of Kuijjer et al. (2019) \doi{10.1016/j.isci.2019.03.021}, as implemented in 'lionessR', and integrates them into multi-omics networks with 'DrDimont' by Hiort et al. (2022) \doi{10.1093/bioinformatics/btac477}. The single-sample multi-omics networks can be compared with each other or with a group network to predict differences in drug response for individual samples or patients.
}
